# Sikhify keeps environment variables next to the code that reads them:
#
#   backend/.env.example   → copy to backend/.env   (server-only: database, auth, email)
#   frontend/.env.example  → copy to frontend/.env  (VITE_* values, public in the bundle)
#
# Never put backend secrets (database URL/token, API keys) in frontend/.env.
# On Vercel, set backend variables in Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# (see docs/VERCEL_DEPLOY.md).
